  "parentCard": {
    "title": "Five little ducks, counted down on your fingers",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "sing",
    "steps": [
      "Sit somewhere comfortable with a grown-up and hold up five fingers. These five fingers are the five little ducks.",
      "Sing the song together. Every time a duck swims away and does not come back, fold that finger down, then count the ducks still standing up, out loud, touching each one as you count.",
      "After each verse, ask each other the same question: how many more ducks were there before than there are now? Count the folded fingers to find out.",
      "Sing it again starting with four ducks, so the numbers land in different places and nothing can be remembered instead of counted.",
      "Finish the other way round. Hold up any number of fingers you like and ask the grown-up how many more they would need to make five, then check it together on your own hand."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Do they count the ducks that are left all over again each time, or do they already know before they look?",
      "When a finger folds down, do they say the new number before they count or after?",
      "Can they say how many more without counting, when the two numbers are close together?"
    ]
  }
